spoint vendors wireweave at client/vendor/wireweave/src/ (importmap 'wireweave' -> /vendor/wireweave/src/index.js). BUG (fixed 50ee3af2) in data.js: a joiner could discover the host, spawn (playerId + snapshot/meshes), have a fully-connected RTCPeerConnection (iceConnectionState/connectionState='connected', signalingState='stable', fsm/peer.state='connected', failCount=0) YET its SCTP RTCDataChannel (label 'wireweave-data') read readyState='closed' with bytes stranded in dc.bufferedAmount, so DataSession.send returns false and the joiner goes mute right after the first snapshot -> 'appears + spawns but cannot play'. Root cause: _wireDataChannel dc.onclose only emitted 'peer-close'; onconnectionstatechange only recovered on pc disconnected/failed/closed, so a LONE datachannel close while the transport stayed 'connected' was never recovered and the dc was never recreated. This was first mis-attributed to a same-browser loopback artifact but the REAL remote host (room 8JHF3, separate machine) reproduced it identically -> genuine wireweave dc-lifecycle bug. FIX: dc.onclose calls _recoverDataChannel(peer,peerPubkey,closedDc) which, when the peer is still tracked (peers.get===peer), the closed dc is the current peer.dc, and pc.connectionState is connected/connecting, recreates the channel: the offerer (auth.pubkey>peerPubkey) does createDataChannel(DC_LABEL,dcOptions)+createOffer+publishSignal; the answerer does _closePeer + _scheduleReconnect to rebuild via a fresh ondatachannel. Deliberate _closePeer/disconnect is unaffected (peer no longer in map). RULE: any WebRTC datachannel needs a close-while-transport-alive recovery path; pc connectionState 'connected' does NOT imply the dc is open. spoint-side companion fixes: host attach catch-up loop (app.js, project/multiplayer-host-bridge-peeropen-catchup) + WireweaveJoinClient send-guard via _hostDcOpen.